    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>Concludes that Soviet advances in sub-megaton yield range are not of major
                    military capability significance. Two attached tables provide a listing of
                    additional December Soviet tests and yield-to-weight ratios on the sub-megaton
                    yield tests. Top Secret. 4 pp. Kennedy Library, National Security Files,
                    Meetings and Memoranda Series, NSAM 205, Box
                    339.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d172-f2" n="2" xml:id="d172-f2-content">
                <p>As the result of dropping these three events, JOE numbers listed in the 20
                    December report (from JOE 124 on) should be re-numbered; JOE 124 becomes JOE
                    121, JOE 125 becomes JOE 122, etc.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d172-f3" n="3" xml:id="d172-f3-content">
                <p>Revised JOE numbers which resulted from dropping of events on 27, 28 and 31 July
                    1962 as nuclear tests.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
